{"kind":"request","text":"R3b: act content must not grow the reusable observation map without limit\n\nThe builder found (3951c80e) that an act's content can choose the subjects that `Further.read` keeps. `listedBy` in derive/observes.ts forms `member:\u003cid\u003e` from act fields: `worker` in the Directory open-task row, `checks[*].checker` in rules-scope publish, and `checkers` in rules-scope-v13. Membership answers an absent member with a valid `memberState: unknown` record. The `reusable` map in packages/scope/src/authority.ts keeps every answered subject that is not `once`, and the map has no capacity check and no eviction. A caller who sends acts that name distinct member IDs grows the map for the life of the run. R3 and R3a bound the signer-key structures only.\n\nInvariant: in one run, the `reusable` map stays within a stated bound for any sequence of acts. An act that names a real member gets the same outcome as on main.\n\nWork:\n1. Read-only proposal first, reported to the planner before any source edit. State three things. First, who can reach the map: after R3's early refusal, does an act from a key without standing still reach `Further.read`? Second, which subjects act content can choose, and which of them Membership's size already bounds. Third, the bound you propose and the reason that it keeps a run consistent. Two candidate designs: do not keep an answer for an absent member, or keep those answers in a separate bounded store that drops its oldest entry, as R3a does for revoked keys. If dropping an entry can change an act's outcome inside one run, name the invariant that forbids the drop.\n2. Witness: one run takes acts that name more distinct absent members than the bound, and the map stays within the bound. A later act that names a real member is admitted with the same result as before. One control: restore today's map and show that the witness fails.\n3. Replace the residual sentence that 3951c80e added to docs/security/threat-model.md with what remains after the fix.\n\nOrder: phase 1, a parallel lane. Step 1 can start now. R3b edits authority.ts, as R3a does, so its source edits start from R3a's frozen head after R3a's review request is filed. R3b does not hold the start of phase 2. Common conditions as in 954bf397: checker review of the exact head before landing, one gate at the final head, and the planner deploys all four Workers after landing.","body":{"conditions":"The reusable observation map stays within a stated bound for any act sequence; an act naming a real member keeps its outcome; proposal before source edit; witness plus one control; threat-model residual updated.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}